CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-013: Screwdriver Antenna — Roll-Up Wire / Trapped Version
CM  2.4m thin wire with inline LC traps for 6m and 2m band isolation
CM  Active model: 10m band with base loading coil
CM  Frequency: 28.000–29.600 MHz (9 points, 0.200 MHz step)
CM
CM  PHYSICAL DESCRIPTION:
CM  This is a roll-up wire version of the screwdriver concept —
CM  a portable/deployable wire antenna with traps for multiband use.
CM  The wire element (radius 0.001m, thin copper wire) is 2.4m long.
CM  Inline traps cut the effective electrical length at higher bands.
CM
CM  TRAP POSITIONS AND FUNCTION:
CM  Trap 1 (2m trap) at z=0.488m — segment 4 of 20:
CM    Physical: parallel LC resonant near 146 MHz.
CM    At 28.5 MHz (10m): far below resonance; trap appears as
CM    small inductive reactance (~+1 ohm at 28.5 MHz). Effect minimal.
CM    At 50 MHz (6m): inductive, ~+20-40 ohm; small loading effect.
CM    At 146 MHz (2m): high impedance — isolates tip section (0-0.488m)
CM    as the radiating element. Effective quarter-wave at 144 MHz.
CM    Modeled as: LD 0 1 4 4  0.05  1.0  (R=0.05, X=+1.0 at 28.5 MHz)
CM
CM  Trap 2 (6m trap) at z=1.40m — segment 12 of 20:
CM    Physical: parallel LC resonant near 51 MHz.
CM    At 28.5 MHz (10m): below resonance; trap is inductive, X~+5 ohm.
CM    Adds small series inductance; slight shift in resonant frequency.
CM    At 50-54 MHz (6m): high impedance — isolates 0-1.40m section
CM    as the radiating element. 1.40m is near QW at 50 MHz.
CM    Modeled as: LD 0 1 12 12  0.1  5.0  (R=0.1, X=+5.0 at 28.5 MHz)
CM
CM  BASE LOADING COIL (10m configuration, active):
CM    This is the variable loading coil (screwdriver motor drive).
CM    Segment 1 of GW1. For 10m, minimal inductance needed.
CM    LD 0 1 1 1  0.107  42.7
CM
CM  WIRE ELEMENT NOTES:
CM  Radius 0.001m = 1mm diameter wire (thin vs screwdriver whip 0.006m).
CM  Thin wire has lower self-capacitance; resonant frequency shifts up
CM  slightly vs thicker element. Adjust loading reactance accordingly.
CM  Segment check: 20 segs over 2.4m = 0.12m/seg.
CM    Trap 1 at seg 4: 4 * 0.12m = 0.48m (near 0.488m — good match)
CM    Trap 2 at seg 12: 12 * 0.12m = 1.44m (nearest to 1.40m target)
CM    Trap 2 is 2.9% off target; acceptable approximation in NEC-2.
CM
CM  BAND BEHAVIOR SUMMARY:
CM  10m: Full 2.4m wire active; traps add small reactive loading.
CM       Base LD provides resonance correction. Active model here.
CM  6m:  6m trap (seg 12) presents high Z; 0 to 1.40m section active.
CM       2m trap (seg 4) is inductive at 50 MHz; small loading effect.
CM       No base loading coil needed (coil bypassed or set to X~0).
CM  2m:  Both traps present high Z at 146 MHz; 0 to 0.488m section
CM       active as QW monopole. Very efficient — no loading coil loss.
CM
CM  ALTERNATIVE CONFIGURATIONS (commented out — swap LD cards):
CM
CM  --- 40m configuration (comment out 10m LD, uncomment below) ---
CM  For 40m (7.000-7.300 MHz): all traps far below resonance.
CM  Both traps appear nearly resistive (small loss) at 7 MHz.
CM  Full 2.4m wire active; base loading coil set to 40m values.
CM  CM  LD 0  1  1  1  3.086  864    <- 40m base loading coil
CM  CM  LD 0  1  4  4  0.05   1.0    <- 2m trap (negligible at 7 MHz)
CM  CM  LD 0  1  12 12  0.1   2.0    <- 6m trap (slightly less X at 7 MHz)
CM  CM  FR 0  7  0  0  7.000  0.050
CM
CM  --- 20m configuration ---
CM  CM  LD 0  1  1  1  1.171  374.8  <- 20m base loading coil
CM  CM  LD 0  1  4  4  0.05   1.0
CM  CM  LD 0  1  12 12  0.1   5.0
CM  CM  FR 0  8  0  0  14.000  0.050
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m WIRE, radius 0.001m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing, radius 0.006m
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM ============================================================
CE
GW 1  20  0 0 0       0 0 2.4     0.001
GW 2   4  0 0 0.005   2.4 0 0.005  0.006
GW 3   4  0 0 0.005  -2.4 0 0.005  0.006
GW 4   4  0 0 0.005   0 2.4 0.005  0.006
GW 5   4  0 0 0.005   0 -2.4 0.005 0.006
GE 1
GN 2 0 0 0  13 0.005
LD 0  1  1  1  0.107  42.7
LD 0  1  4  4  0.05   1.0
LD 0  1  12 12  0.1   5.0
EX 0  1  1  0  1  0
FR 0  9  0  0  28.000  0.200
RP 0  37  73  1000  0  0  5  5
EN
